	'ka952be8a' => 'Visit the showroom ↗',
	'kaa11a5a3' => 'This residential project transformed an awkward structural alcove beneath a flight of stairs into a dedicated evening reading nook. Space constraints ruled out a freestanding floor lamp, so we specified a single Lantern Wall Light at €310. Mounted directly onto the lime-plaster wall, its brass swing-arm mechanism allows the reader to pull the light forward over an armchair or push it flush against the wall when not in use. The natural linen cone shade shields peripheral glare, casting direct 2700K illumination solely onto open books.',
	'kab482bb6' => 'To ensure our pieces last for decades, we operate an active repair bench at Steenkade 14. Here, vintage lamps are rewired from €65, and replacement shades or cords are fitted to ensure that well-made lighting stays in service across generations.',
	'kacf38646' => 'Kitchen tables, glare-free and downward ↗',
